# Flux Engine — Allowed Git SSH Signers (.github/allowed_signers)
#
# Used by `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/verify_release.sh` to
# cryptographically verify signed release tags (`vX.Y.Z*`) and signed commits:
#
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=.github/allowed_signers verify-tag v1.0.3
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=.github/allowed_signers verify-commit HEAD
#
# Format (see `man ssh-keygen`, ALLOWED SIGNERS):
#   <principal> namespaces="git" <key-type> <base64-public-key>
#
# Privacy rule: ALWAYS use the pseudonymous GitHub noreply principal below;
# NEVER commit personal email addresses or real names into this file.
#
# Non-dry-run tag releases in `.github/workflows/release.yml` FAIL CLOSED until
# at least one active (uncommented) maintainer public key line is registered
# below. See `SIGNING.md` for full key generation and hardware FIDO2 setup.
#
# Example — Option A (Hardware FIDO2 / YubiKey 5 resident key, recommended):
# 149847121+TheApathy@users.noreply.github.com namespaces="git" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAAGnNrLXNzaC1lZDI1NTE5QG9wZW5zc2guY29tAAAA...
#
